                                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource BaseText}" FontWeight="SemiBold" Margin="0,0,0,2">
                                        v1.4.0  ·  Build 77 / 80 fix — MKV Artwork via MKVPropEdit
                                    </TextBlock>
                                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource BaseText}" Foreground="{DynamicResource ForegroundMutedBrush}" Margin="8,0,0,12" TextWrapping="Wrap">
                                        New service: MkvPropEditService.cs.
                                        Detects mkvpropedit (MKVToolNix) at startup from
                                        standard install paths, Scoop/Chocolatey, portable
                                        folder alongside the EXE, and PATH.
                                        When detected, MKV artwork is written as a proper
                                        Matroska attachment named "cover.jpg" using
                                        mkvpropedit instead of TagLib#. This format is
                                        correctly recognised by Plex, Jellyfin, Emby, and
                                        VLC. TagLib# stored artwork as a generic binary
                                        attachment which many players ignored.
                                        Applied to the temp file before atomic replace —
                                        source file is never touched until the complete
                                        write (tags + artwork) is verified.
                                        Fallback: if mkvpropedit is unavailable or fails,
                                        TagLib# artwork write is used silently. Non-fatal
                                        mkvpropedit warnings are logged to Processing Log
                                        but do not abort the embed operation.
                                        Settings tab → MKV Artwork Engine shows whether
                                        mkvpropedit was detected and its path.
                                        Install: mkvtoolnix.download/downloads.html
                                        No UI or workflow change — transparent to user.
                                    </TextBlock>

