                                        Move/Copy saved settings fields were blank in the
                                        Settings tab despite the status bar showing the
                                        correct values. Root cause: AppSettings is a plain
                                        POCO — WPF binding evaluates Settings.LastCopy*
                                        once on startup and never refreshes. Fixed with
                                        SavedCopyDestination and SavedConflictMode proxy
                                        properties on MainViewModel that raise
                                        PropertyChanged whenever the underlying setting
                                        changes. All four code paths that write the setting
                                        (auto-save, manual save, clear, startup restore)
                                        now raise both proxy notifications.
                                    </TextBlock>

                                    <!-- ═══ Recent builds — v1.4.0 Builds 46–55 ═══════════════ -->

                                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource BaseText}" FontWeight="SemiBold" Margin="0,0,0,2">
                                        v1.4.0  ·  Build 55 — Move/Copy Persistence · Cover Art Fix
                                    </TextBlock>
                                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource BaseText}" Foreground="{DynamicResource ForegroundMutedBrush}" Margin="8,0,0,12" TextWrapping="Wrap">
                                        Move/Copy persistent settings. CopyDestination and
                                        ConflictMode were ephemeral (reset to empty/Skip on
                                        every restart). Both now persist to config.json
                                        (LastCopyDestination, LastConflictMode) on every change
                                        and restore silently on startup. Settings tab: new
                                        "📦 Move / Copy — Saved Settings" GroupBox shows
                                        current saved values, a Clear button, and a manual
                                        Save button. Status bar confirms when saved.
                                        Library cover art fix. DataGrid row virtualization
                                        was the root cause: WPF only materialises row
                                        containers for visible rows. When entries were added
                                        while on another tab, off-screen rows were never
                                        created, so CoverArt bindings never evaluated and
                                        the BytesToImageSourceConverter never ran. Switching
                                        to Log tab forced a DataGrid layout pass that
                                        materialised all rows. Fixed with
                                        EnableRowVirtualization="False" and
                                        VirtualizingPanel.IsVirtualizing="False" — all rows
                                        are realised immediately so covers appear on first
                                        render regardless of which tab was active during load.
                                        Export CSV retained. Not redundant — CSV opens in any
                                        text editor or script without Excel. XLSX requires
                                        Excel-compatible software. Both formats serve
                                        distinct audiences.
                                    </TextBlock>

                                    <!-- ═══ Recent builds — v1.4.0 Builds 46–54 ═══════════════ -->

                                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource BaseText}" FontWeight="SemiBold" Margin="0,0,0,2">
                                        v1.4.0  ·  Build 54 — Covers · XLSX Export · Settings Field Fix · Help Tab Updated
                                    </TextBlock>
                                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource BaseText}" Foreground="{DynamicResource ForegroundMutedBrush}" Margin="8,0,0,12" TextWrapping="Wrap">
                                        Cover art restored in Library tab. Build 53 switched
                                        LibraryScanService to ReadMetadataFast which skips artwork,
                                        breaking cover display. Fixed with a background artwork
                                        pass (LoadArtworkAsync) that runs after the scan populates
                                        the grid — scan speed is preserved and covers load live
                                        as each file is read. LibraryEntry.CoverArt is now a
                                        notifying property so DataGrid cells refresh when artwork
