                                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource BaseText}" FontWeight="SemiBold" Margin="0,0,0,2">
                                        v1.3.4  ·  Build 46 — Full Codebase Audit (Second Pass)
                                    </TextBlock>
                                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource BaseText}" Foreground="{DynamicResource ForegroundMutedBrush}" Margin="8,0,0,12" TextWrapping="Wrap">
                                        Seven issues found and fixed across a second comprehensive audit:
                                        WatchFolderService._knownPaths (race condition): HashSet is
                                        not thread-safe. FSW.OnCreated fires on the thread pool
                                        while DispatcherTimer.Tick fires on the UI thread — both
                                        called DispatchDetect concurrently, causing silent
                                        deduplication failures. Replaced with ConcurrentDictionary.
                                        WatchFolderService.PollFolder (UI thread block):
                                        Directory.EnumerateFiles ran synchronously on the UI thread
                                        via DispatcherTimer — could freeze the interface for seconds
                                        on large or network folders. Offloaded to Task.Run.
                                        NfoExportService: no CancellationToken — bulk NFO exports
                                        of hundreds of files could not be stopped. Added ct param,
                                        threaded through loop and WriteAllTextAsync.
                                        FindDuplicates() async void: unhandled exceptions were
                                        silently swallowed. Also IsBusy=true was set before
                                        BeginOperation(), meaning Cancel used a stale CTS.
                                        Extracted to FindDuplicatesAsync(); shell catches exceptions.
                                        BeginOperation() now called first.
                                        ToggleLockCurrentFile() async void: same async void
                                        exception-swallow pattern. Extracted to
                                        ToggleLockCurrentFileAsync() with shell wrapper.
                                        AutoSearchAsync ct:default: auto-search passed
                                        CancellationToken.None to TMDB/OMDB calls — pressing
                                        Cancel didn't stop in-progress API requests. Fixed to
                                        pass the real ct parameter.
                                        VideoFile.IsReadOnly (per-render disk hit): the getter
                                        created new FileInfo(FilePath) on every call — WPF binding
                                        evaluated this on every render pass. With 2,400 files this
                                        caused thousands of filesystem stat calls per second.
                                        Added _isReadOnlyCached nullable bool; invalidated by
                                        TrySetReadOnly and new RefreshReadOnly() method.
                                    </TextBlock>

                                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource BaseText}" FontWeight="SemiBold" Margin="0,0,0,2">
                                        v1.3.4  ·  Build 45 — Watch Folder Remaining Fixes
                                    </TextBlock>
                                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource BaseText}" Foreground="{DynamicResource ForegroundMutedBrush}" Margin="8,0,0,12" TextWrapping="Wrap">
                                        Three remaining Watch Folder issues resolved after build 44:
                                        (1) Batch embed path did not clear the yellow IsNewFile
                                        highlight on success — files processed via Batch Process
                                        stayed highlighted until the app was restarted.
                                        (2) Batch rename path did not call AddKnownPath(newPath)
                                        after a successful rename — the poll timer would re-detect
                                        renamed files as new arrivals on its next tick.
                                        (3) RefreshFilesAsync (Refresh button) did not re-seed
                                        the watch service knownPaths after reloading the file list
                                        — every refreshed file was re-fired as a new arrival.
                                        All three paths now fully consistent with the single-file
                                        embed path which was already correct.
                                    </TextBlock>

                                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource BaseText}" FontWeight="SemiBold" Margin="0,0,0,2">
                                        v1.3.4  ·  Build 44 — Watch Folder Fixes · Library Watch
                                    </TextBlock>
                                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource BaseText}" Foreground="{DynamicResource ForegroundMutedBrush}" Margin="8,0,0,12" TextWrapping="Wrap">
                                        Watch Folder — four root bugs fixed:
                                        (1) TryAddFile ran TagLib# on the UI thread (100–500ms
                                        per file). Now dispatched to a background Task.Run with
                                        InvokeAsync(Background) — same pattern as AddFolder.
                                        Multiple simultaneous FSW events no longer freeze the UI.
                                        (2) IsNewFile (yellow highlight) was never cleared after
                                        a successful single-file embed. Now set to false in the
                                        embed success path.
                                        (3) After AddFolder loaded files, those paths weren't
                                        registered with the watch service — poll timer re-fired
                                        them as new arrivals on the next tick. Fixed.
                                        (4) After rename, old filename stayed in knownPaths and
                                        new filename was never registered — renamed file appeared
                                        as new arrival. Fixed by calling AddKnownPath(newPath)
                                        in the single-file rename path.
                                        Library Watch (new — Settings tab):
                                        New "📚 Library Watch" group in Settings. Toggle "Watch
                                        Library folder for new files" with configurable poll
                                        interval. Uses a second WatchFolderService instance on
                                        LibraryFolderPath. New files are built as full LibraryEntry
                                        objects (title, year, genre, artwork, codec, resolution)
                                        via BuildSingleEntryAsync and added to the Library grid
                                        automatically — no re-scan required.
                                        Green "👁 Watching" badge in Library tab footer when active.
                                        Known paths re-seeded after each full scan. Folder changes
                                        and load-from-Library events update the watch automatically.
                                    </TextBlock>

                                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource BaseText}" FontWeight="SemiBold" Margin="0,0,0,2">
                                        v1.3.4  ·  Build 43 — Full Codebase Audit
                                    </TextBlock>
                                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource BaseText}" Foreground="{DynamicResource ForegroundMutedBrush}" Margin="8,0,0,12" TextWrapping="Wrap">
                                        Comprehensive audit across all services and ViewModels:
                                        Dead field: AppSettings.ImdbApiKey removed — never read,
                                        written to every config.json silently.
                                        FileRenameService: {Rating} token added. Rename pattern
                                        now supports {Title} {Year} {Genre} {Director} {Rating}
                                        {ImdbId} {TmdbId}. Settings hint label updated.
                                        DuplicateDetectorService: local ephemeral hash Dictionary
                                        promoted to static session ConcurrentDictionary — hashes
                                        persist across calls. ClearHashCache() called after every
                                        successful embed so stale entries never give false positives.
                                        RecoveryService.Resume: File.Replace throws cross-volume —
                                        added IOException catch → File.Copy + File.Delete fallback
                                        so Resume works on network paths and junctions.
                                        ValidateKeysAsync: Task.Delay(4000) with no CancellationToken
                                        left IsBusy stuck true if another operation started during
                                        the 4-second flash window. Fixed with try/catch.
                                        Help tab: Features section and Recommended Workflow fully
