                                    </TextBlock>

                                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource BaseText}" FontWeight="SemiBold" Margin="0,0,0,2">
                                        v1.3.4  ·  Build 42 — Write Engine Overhaul
                                    </TextBlock>
                                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource BaseText}" Foreground="{DynamicResource ForegroundMutedBrush}" Margin="8,0,0,12" TextWrapping="Wrap">
                                        Three root causes behind the batch write failures identified
                                        and fixed:
                                        (1) Artwork stripping in batch: files never selected had
                                        ArtworkBytes=null (lazy load not triggered). Write engine
                                        was embedding null, silently removing existing cover art.
                                        Fixed: write engine reads existing artwork from file before
                                        writing if metadata has none. Batch path pre-loads artwork
                                        for each file before calling write.
                                        (2) WriteTagsSync returned true unconditionally — exceptions
                                        from tagFile.Save() were caught as generic "tag write failed"
                                        with no useful message. Replaced with WriteTagsSafe() which
                                        returns (bool, string?) so the real error reaches the log.
                                        (3) Temp file sanity check added: if TagLib# output is less
                                        than half the original size, the write is rejected before
                                        File.Replace is called.
                                        OperationCanceledException now propagates correctly through
                                        the write pipeline. Diagnostics include both first and last
                                        attempt errors.
                                    </TextBlock>

