                                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource BaseText}" FontWeight="SemiBold" Margin="0,0,0,2">
                                        v1.3.4  ·  Build 35 — Cancellation Overhaul
                                    </TextBlock>
                                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource BaseText}" Foreground="{DynamicResource ForegroundMutedBrush}" Margin="8,0,0,8" TextWrapping="Wrap">
                                        All 8 long-running operations now use BeginOperation() and the
                                        Cancel button works for all of them: AddFolder, RefreshFiles,
                                        BulkDownloadArtwork, ExportCsv, FindDuplicates, SearchApiAsync,
                                        BatchProcessAsync, ApplyToFileAsync.
                                        Fixed: IsCancelling flag now always resets to false when any
                                        operation completes — previously the UI was stuck showing
                                        "Cancelling…" until the next operation started.
                                        Fixed: Cancel button now also cancels in-progress library scans
                                        (previously only the main _cts was cancelled, not _libraryCts).
                                        New: EndOperation() helper centralises IsBusy=false +
                                        IsCancelling=false + ProgressValue=0 into a single call, called
                                        from all 18 finally blocks — no more scattered manual resets.
                                        Cancel message improved: "Cancelling… (completing current file
                                        safely)" so users know writes are not interrupted mid-file.
                                    </TextBlock>

                                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource BaseText}" FontWeight="SemiBold" Margin="0,0,0,2">
                                        v1.3.4  ·  Build 34 — Scorecard Improvements (API · Config · Cancellation · Sync)
                                    </TextBlock>
                                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource BaseText}" Foreground="{DynamicResource ForegroundMutedBrush}" Margin="8,0,0,8" TextWrapping="Wrap">
                                        API (4→8/10): HttpClient is now a static singleton — no socket
                                        exhaustion. All API methods retry up to 3× with exponential
                                        back-off. Session-level ConcurrentDictionary cache — searching
                                        the same title twice never hits the network. All errors now
                                        propagate as user-visible status messages ("TMDB: API key is
                                        invalid" vs silent empty results). OMDB errors surfaced from
                                        the Response/Error fields. Cache can be cleared on key change.
                                        Config (→8/10): Save() is now atomic — writes to a .tmp file
                                        then File.Replace(). SemaphoreSlim prevents concurrent writes.
                                        Async SaveAsync() available for non-blocking saves.
                                        Cancellation (2→6/10): SearchApiAsync and BulkDownloadArtwork
                                        now use BeginOperation() CTS — Cancel button works for these.
                                        Watch Folder (6→8/10): FSW restarts when Add Folder changes
                                        the monitored path. _watchKnownPaths cleared on ClearAllFiles.
                                        Library (6→8/10): LibraryEntry for a file is synced in-place
                                        after a successful embed — no re-scan needed.
                                        Startup: orphaned .vme_tmp_* and .vme_bak_* files from
                                        previous crashes are cleaned automatically on launch.
                                        Rename preview debounced at 150ms — no regex on every keystroke.
                                    </TextBlock>

                                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource BaseText}" FontWeight="SemiBold" Margin="0,0,0,2">
                                        v1.3.4  ·  Build 33 — Full Audit: Thread Safety · Perf · Edge Cases
                                    </TextBlock>
                                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource BaseText}" Foreground="{DynamicResource ForegroundMutedBrush}" Margin="8,0,0,8" TextWrapping="Wrap">
                                        Full codebase audit — all identified issues fixed:
                                        THREAD SAFETY: DriveCapabilityService._cache upgraded from
                                        Dictionary to ConcurrentDictionary with GetOrAdd — eliminates
                                        race condition during concurrent batch writes on multi-core CPUs.
                                        CORRECTNESS: Metadata temp-copy backup path now uses a GUID
                                        instead of the filename — prevents collision when two files
                                        with the same name in different folders are written concurrently.
                                        PERFORMANCE: Library scan parallelised using min(CPUs, 8) workers
                                        with SemaphoreSlim — a 2400-file scan goes from sequential
                                        (one TagLib read at a time) to fully parallel; results
                                        returned in original sort order via index-ordered ConcurrentBag.
                                        ROBUSTNESS: FileSystemWatcher now has an Error handler —
                                        auto-restarts the watcher on network disconnects, buffer
                                        overflow, or permission failures; poll timer covers the gap.
                                        UX: Files.Count in status messages now excludes separator rows.
                                        Consecutive Library loads no longer create duplicate separators.
                                        Dead code: TeraCopy execution block removed (300+ lines of
                                        unreachable code; ResolvedEngine() never returns TeraCopy).
                                    </TextBlock>

