                                        engine list with a visible UAC warning. The engine detection
                                        banner now clearly states which engine Auto will use. Radio
                                        buttons updated with tooltips explaining each engine's behaviour.
                                    </TextBlock>

                                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource BaseText}" FontWeight="SemiBold" Margin="0,0,0,2">
                                        v1.3.4  ·  Build 28 — TeraCopy Success Detection Fix
                                    </TextBlock>
                                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource BaseText}" Foreground="{DynamicResource ForegroundMutedBrush}" Margin="8,0,0,8" TextWrapping="Wrap">
                                        Fixed TeraCopy reporting "1 failed" when the transfer actually
                                        succeeded. Root cause: TeraCopy 3.x returns exit code 1 (not 0)
                                        when any file was skipped due to conflict policy — this is normal
                                        behaviour, not an error. The app was treating exit code 1 as
                                        failure. Fix: success is now determined by verifying which files
                                        actually arrived at the destination rather than relying on the
                                        exit code. Exit code 1 = "completed with skips" is treated as
                                        success. Only exit codes above 1 indicate a hard error (access
                                        denied, out of space, etc.) and are reported as failures.
                                        Note: TeraCopy's UAC prompt on every launch is caused by its own
                                        requireAdministrator manifest — not controllable from external
                                        apps. PowerShell launching would not bypass this.
                                        FastCopy confirmed: does have native move (/cmd=move + /wipe_del
                                        ensures copy is verified before source deletion).
                                    </TextBlock>

                                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource BaseText}" FontWeight="SemiBold" Margin="0,0,0,2">
                                        v1.3.4  ·  Build 27 — FastCopy Move Fix · TeraCopy Count Fix · Engine Status Messages
                                    </TextBlock>
                                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource BaseText}" Foreground="{DynamicResource ForegroundMutedBrush}" Margin="8,0,0,8" TextWrapping="Wrap">
                                        FastCopy move operation fixed: removed /no_confirm_del flag which
                                        caused exit code -1 on FastCopy versions that don't support it.
                                        Added /wipe_del for move operations (verifies copy before deletion).
                                        TeraCopy result counting fixed: Move operations no longer count
                                        successfully moved files as "failed" due to source deletion.
                                        All three engines now show clear, consistent status bar messages:
                                        "TeraCopy — Copy Operation Successful · 5 file(s) (3.2 GB)"
                                        "FastCopy — Move Operation Failed · exited with code -1"
                                        "Custom Fast — Copy Operation Successful · 5 file(s) · 5 size-verified"
                                    </TextBlock>

                                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource BaseText}" FontWeight="SemiBold" Margin="0,0,0,2">
                                        v1.3.4  ·  Build 26 — Full Audit: Memory, Resource &amp; Engine Fixes
                                    </TextBlock>
                                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource BaseText}" Foreground="{DynamicResource ForegroundMutedBrush}" Margin="8,0,0,8" TextWrapping="Wrap">
                                        Full codebase audit — all identified issues fixed:
                                        MEMORY: Large-file parallel copy now uses ArrayPool to rent 64MB
                                        buffers instead of allocating new byte arrays per chunk, eliminating
                                        GC pressure during large batch copies (was: up to 1GB heap churn).
                                        RESOURCE LEAK: MonitorDestinationAsync timer now always stops in a
                                        finally block even if WaitForExitAsync throws or is cancelled.
                                        RESOURCE LEAK: MainWindow now correctly unsubscribes all ViewModel
                                        events on close including WriteFailedDetailed and PropertyChanged
                                        (stored handler reference). Popout preview closed on window unload.
                                        DRIVE SAFETY: isLocalSSD() fixed — previously used DriveType.Fixed
                                        which includes spinning HDDs, causing 4 parallel chunk workers on
                                        HDDs (seek thrashing). Now uses DriveCapabilityService IOCTL.
                                        CLEANUP: Removed unused speedBytes/speedStart variables. Removed
                                        stale duplicate XML doc comment on RunExternalAsync.
                                        TERACOPY NOTE: UAC prompt on every launch is caused by TeraCopy's
                                        own requireAdministrator manifest — not fixable from the app side.
                                        Use Custom Fast (Recommended) to avoid UAC entirely.
                                    </TextBlock>

                                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource BaseText}" FontWeight="SemiBold" Margin="0,0,0,2">
                                        v1.3.4  ·  Build 25 — Custom Fast Real-Time Progress &amp; Speed Display
                                    </TextBlock>
                                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource BaseText}" Foreground="{DynamicResource ForegroundMutedBrush}" Margin="8,0,0,8" TextWrapping="Wrap">
                                        Custom Fast (Recommended) engine now shows byte-accurate real-time
                                        progress in the status bar matching the style of File Organizer:
                                        "Copying... 94.2% (8/13) · 9.43 GB / 14.31 GB · 423 MB/s · movie.mp4"
                                        Includes rolling transfer speed updated every 500ms, percentage with
                                        one decimal place, files done/total, bytes transferred/total, and
                                        the name of the file currently being copied. Progress bar is
                                        byte-accurate (not file-count-based) for smooth visual feedback
                                        even when files vary greatly in size.
                                    </TextBlock>

                                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource BaseText}" FontWeight="SemiBold" Margin="0,0,0,2">
                                        v1.3.4  ·  Build 24 — TeraCopy Smart Destination Quoting
                                    </TextBlock>
                                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource BaseText}" Foreground="{DynamicResource ForegroundMutedBrush}" Margin="8,0,0,8" TextWrapping="Wrap">
                                        Fixed TeraCopy erroring on forward-slash destination paths.
                                        Smart quoting now handles all destination types: paths without
                                        spaces use unquoted *D:\ (backslash is only special before a
                                        quote character — never in bare unquoted text); paths with
                                        spaces use *"D:\My Movies" after trimming the trailing backslash
                                        so there is no backslash-before-quote issue. Covers drive roots,
                                        subfolders, and UNC paths in all cases.
                                    </TextBlock>

                                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource BaseText}" FontWeight="SemiBold" Margin="0,0,0,2">
                                        v1.3.4  ·  Build 23 — TeraCopy Forward-Slash Destination Fix
                                    </TextBlock>
                                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource BaseText}" Foreground="{DynamicResource ForegroundMutedBrush}" Margin="8,0,0,8" TextWrapping="Wrap">
                                        Fixed TeraCopy using the last source file as the destination instead
                                        of the actual destination folder. Root cause: TeraCopy 3.x ignores
                                        the *"D:\\" argument entirely (backslash quoting confusion) and falls
                                        back to treating the last source path as its target. Fix: destination
                                        is now passed as *"D:/" using forward slashes. Windows accepts / as
                                        a path separator, and "D:/" has no trailing-backslash quoting issue.
                                        TeraCopy 3.x correctly resolves *D:/ as the D:\ drive root.
                                    </TextBlock>

                                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource BaseText}" FontWeight="SemiBold" Margin="0,0,0,2">
                                        v1.3.4  ·  Build 22 — TeraCopy Destination Trailing Backslash Fix
                                    </TextBlock>
                                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource BaseText}" Foreground="{DynamicResource ForegroundMutedBrush}" Margin="8,0,0,8" TextWrapping="Wrap">
                                        Fixed TeraCopy showing Target as "*D:" (Unavailable). The destination
                                        needs a trailing backslash for TeraCopy to resolve it as a folder,
                                        but quoting rules mean "D:" is broken (" = escaped quote). Fix:
                                        use "D:\" — two backslashes before the closing quote produce one
                                        literal backslash, so TeraCopy receives *D:\ correctly.
                                    </TextBlock>

                                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource BaseText}" FontWeight="SemiBold" Margin="0,0,0,2">
                                        v1.3.4  ·  Build 21 — TeraCopy Direct Argument Fix
                                    </TextBlock>
                                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource BaseText}" Foreground="{DynamicResource ForegroundMutedBrush}" Margin="8,0,0,8" TextWrapping="Wrap">
                                        Fixed TeraCopy copying the temp list .txt file itself instead of the
                                        actual video files. Root cause: TeraCopy 3.x CLI does not support
                                        the @listfile syntax — it treats "@path.txt" as a literal source
                                        file path, not a list reference. Fix: source files are now passed
                                        as individual quoted arguments directly on the command line.
                                        For large batches, files are automatically chunked into groups
                                        of ~28,000 characters to stay within the Windows command-line
                                        limit, with TeraCopy called sequentially per chunk.
                                    </TextBlock>

                                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource BaseText}" FontWeight="SemiBold" Margin="0,0,0,2">
                                        v1.3.4  ·  Build 20 — TeraCopy Destination Path Fix
                                    </TextBlock>
                                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource BaseText}" Foreground="{DynamicResource ForegroundMutedBrush}" Margin="8,0,0,8" TextWrapping="Wrap">
                                        Fixed TeraCopy reporting "More space is required: 1 B" despite ample
                                        free space. Root cause: destination paths ending with a backslash
                                        (e.g. D:\) were quoted as *"D:\" — the \" inside quotes is parsed
                                        by the Windows argument parser as an escaped quote, corrupting the
                                        path TeraCopy received. Fix: trailing backslash stripped before
                                        quoting so TeraCopy receives *"D:" which it resolves correctly.
                                    </TextBlock>

                                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource BaseText}" FontWeight="SemiBold" Margin="0,0,0,2">
                                        v1.3.4  ·  Build 19 — Race Condition Fix: Apply to Correct File
                                    </TextBlock>
                                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource BaseText}" Foreground="{DynamicResource ForegroundMutedBrush}" Margin="8,0,0,8" TextWrapping="Wrap">
                                        Fixed a race condition in Apply + Embed + Rename where clicking a
                                        different file mid-operation caused the rename to apply to the newly
                                        selected file instead of the original. Root cause: SelectedFile and
                                        EditingMetadata were accessed via live properties through multiple
                                        await suspension points. Fix: both are now snapshotted into local
                                        variables (targetFile, metadataToWrite) at the very start of the
                                        method before any await, so every subsequent operation — read-only
                                        check, lock diagnosis, write, rename, status update — uses the
                                        captured state and is completely unaffected by UI selection changes.
                                    </TextBlock>

                                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource BaseText}" FontWeight="SemiBold" Margin="0,0,0,2">
                                        v1.3.4  ·  Build 18 — Multi-Threaded Writes · TeraCopy Full UI · Concurrent Write Service
                                    </TextBlock>
                                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource BaseText}" Foreground="{DynamicResource ForegroundMutedBrush}" Margin="8,0,0,8" TextWrapping="Wrap">
                                        Batch embed uses multiple concurrent write workers, automatically scaled
                                        to drive type and CPU: NVMe=8, SATA SSD=6, USB SSD=4, HDD=2, Network=1.
                                        WriteThreadService queries the same DriveCapabilityService IOCTL as the
                                        folder scanner. Auto vs manual concurrency in Settings → Performance.
                                        TagLib# is safe for concurrent use across different files — each write
                                        creates its own instance so parallel calls never interfere.
                                        TeraCopy now launches with its full visible window so you can see
                                        TeraCopy's own detailed per-file progress and verification results
                                        while the app status bar simultaneously updates via destination-folder
                                        monitoring. FastCopy remains headless with /no_ui.
                                        Destination-folder monitoring shared between both engines via
                                        MonitorDestinationAsync for cleaner, consistent progress reporting.
                                    </TextBlock>

                                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource BaseText}" FontWeight="SemiBold" Margin="0,0,0,2">
                                        v1.3.3  ·  Build 17 — Write &amp; Rename Bug Fixes
                                    </TextBlock>
                                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource BaseText}" Foreground="{DynamicResource ForegroundMutedBrush}" Margin="8,0,0,8" TextWrapping="Wrap">
                                        Fixed critical write failure for files with uppercase extensions (e.g. .MP4).
                                        The temp-copy file now preserves the original extension so TagLib# can
                                        correctly identify the container format — previously it saw .vme_tmp_xxx
                                        as an unknown type and threw "File not writeable", causing both write
                                        passes to fail and blocking the rename entirely.
                                        Fixed rename skipping files where the extension case differed (.MP4 → .mp4):
                                        NTFS case-only renames now use a two-step move via a temp name.
                                        Extension case is now preserved as-is from the original file.
                                    </TextBlock>

                                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource BaseText}" FontWeight="SemiBold" Margin="0,0,0,2">
                                        v1.3.3  ·  Build 16 — Real-Time Progress for TeraCopy &amp; FastCopy
                                    </TextBlock>
                                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource BaseText}" Foreground="{DynamicResource ForegroundMutedBrush}" Margin="8,0,0,8" TextWrapping="Wrap">
                                        TeraCopy and FastCopy now show real-time byte-accurate progress in the
                                        status bar by monitoring the destination folder every 300ms — no more
                                        fake pulsing progress bar. Status bar shows files done, bytes transferred,
                                        and the currently-copying filename. FastCopy log file is parsed at
                                        completion for exact Copy/Skip/Error counts.
                                    </TextBlock>

                                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource BaseText}" FontWeight="SemiBold" Margin="0,0,0,2">
                                        v1.3.3  ·  Build 15 — Temp-Copy as Primary Write Method
                                    </TextBlock>
                                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource BaseText}" Foreground="{DynamicResource ForegroundMutedBrush}" Margin="8,0,0,8" TextWrapping="Wrap">
                                        Temp-copy atomic replace is now the primary write method for every file
                                        (not just a fallback). This means every embed is crash-safe, lock-safe,
                                        and corruption-safe by default — the original is never touched until the
                                        atomic NTFS swap. In-place write is retained as a fallback only when the
                                        drive has insufficient free space for the temp copy (checked before each
                                        write). The Processing Log shows "Done (in-place)" when the fallback
                                        was used, and "Done" for the normal temp-copy path.
                                    </TextBlock>

                                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource BaseText}" FontWeight="SemiBold" Margin="0,0,0,2">
                                        v1.3.3  ·  Build 14 — Temp-Copy Write Fallback
                                    </TextBlock>
                                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource BaseText}" Foreground="{DynamicResource ForegroundMutedBrush}" Margin="8,0,0,8" TextWrapping="Wrap">
                                        Added a temp-copy + atomic NTFS replace fallback when the standard in-place
                                        TagLib# write fails after all retries. Mirrors the method used by TagScanner:
                                        copies the original to a temp file, writes tags there (no lock contention),
                                        then atomically swaps temp → original via File.Replace(). Resolves write
                                        failures caused by Windows Search, antivirus, or media players holding the
                                        file open. If the fallback also fails, full diagnostics are shown.
                                    </TextBlock>

                                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource BaseText}" FontWeight="SemiBold" Margin="0,0,0,2">
                                        v1.3.3  ·  Build 13 — Write Error Diagnostics · File Row Colour Coding
                                    </TextBlock>
                                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource BaseText}" Foreground="{DynamicResource ForegroundMutedBrush}" Margin="8,0,0,8" TextWrapping="Wrap">
                                        File row colour coding per session: green = written OK, pink = write failed,
                                        default = not yet processed. Colours clear when a file is successfully
                                        re-embedded or the session ends.
                                        Verbose Write Errors (Settings → Write Error Diagnostics): when enabled,
                                        a detailed dialog explains exactly why a write failed with 7 diagnostic
                                        categories (read-only, file lock, NTFS permissions, network volume,
                                        optical media, format unsupported, unknown). Each dialog includes a
                                        "Copy to Clipboard" button for sharing with support.
                                        Batch processing now also sets per-file WriteStatus for colour coding.
                                        Colour legend added to the Write Error Diagnostics section in Settings.
                                    </TextBlock>

                                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource BaseText}" FontWeight="SemiBold" Margin="0,0,0,2">
                                        v1.3.2  ·  Build 12 — FastCopy/TeraCopy CLI Fixes · Progress Pulse · Copy Behaviour
                                    </TextBlock>
                                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource BaseText}" Foreground="{DynamicResource ForegroundMutedBrush}" Margin="8,0,0,8" TextWrapping="Wrap">
                                        FastCopy: fixed /cmd=copy (invalid) → correct command map per conflict mode.
                                        FastCopy and TeraCopy: source file lists now written to a temp file to avoid
                                        command-line length limits and UAC elevation prompts.
                                        UseShellExecute=false prevents UAC dialogs when launching external tools.
                                        Progress bar pulses with elapsed-seconds counter during external transfers.
                                        Copy operation no longer reloads the file list (source files stay).
                                        Move operation removes transferred files and refreshes the source folder.
                                        Space Analysis section added to Move/Copy tab with drive usage breakdown.
                                        File Conflict Resolution dropdown: Skip, Overwrite, Overwrite if Newer, Rename.
                                        Built-in engine renamed to "Custom Fast (Recommended)".
                                    </TextBlock>

                                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource BaseText}" FontWeight="SemiBold" Margin="0,0,0,2">
                                        v1.3.1  ·  Build 11 — Ratings · Duplicate Hashing · Write Retry · UI Polish
                                    </TextBlock>
                                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource BaseText}" Foreground="{DynamicResource ForegroundMutedBrush}" Margin="8,0,0,8" TextWrapping="Wrap">
                                        IMDB rating displayed as stars (★★★½☆ 7.1/10) in Raw Data and Retrieved Data tabs.
                                        Ratings fetched from TMDB (vote_average) and OMDB (imdbRating) with vote counts.
                                        Rating stored as [VME:RATING=7.1] marker in the tag Comment field.
                                        Genres sorted alphabetically on import and on write.
                                        Full Cast field is now multi-line and scrollable — no text is cut off.
                                        Metadata write retry with back-off: up to 3 attempts, 500ms×attempt delay.
                                        Duplicate detection upgraded to async with real-time hashing progress.
                                        Tab titles capitalised: RAW DATA, RETRIEVED DATA, MOVE / COPY, SETTINGS, HELP, LOG.
                                        Clear Search Results button added to Retrieved Data tab.
                                        Preview Popout: ⧉ button next to Play/Stop opens a modeless floating player.
                                        Apply + Embed + Rename uses the exact form fields shown — edits made after
                                        retrieving metadata are preserved and embedded correctly.
                                    </TextBlock>

                                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource BaseText}" FontWeight="SemiBold" Margin="0,0,0,2">
                                        v1.3.0  ·  Build 10 — File Lock / Unlock
                                    </TextBlock>
                                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource BaseText}" Foreground="{DynamicResource ForegroundMutedBrush}" Margin="8,0,0,8" TextWrapping="Wrap">
                                        Fixes the "File not writeable" error caused by Windows read-only attribute.
                                        Lock icon (🔒 red / 🔓 grey) on every file row reflects live disk state.
                                        Red warning banner appears in Raw Data tab when a locked file is selected,
                                        with an inline Unlock button to clear the attribute in one click.
                                        🔒 Locked / 🔓 Unlocked toggle button next to Apply + Embed + Rename.
                                        Batch 🔒 Lock and 🔓 Unlock buttons in the toolbar apply to all selected files.
                                        Read-only guard in ApplyToFileAsync blocks embedding before TagLib# is called,
                                        fires a ReadOnlyFileBlocked event, and logs the block to the Processing Log.
                                    </TextBlock>

                                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource BaseText}" FontWeight="SemiBold" Margin="0,0,0,2">
                                        v1.3.0  ·  Build 9 — Full Feature Release (25 additions)
                                    </TextBlock>
                                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource BaseText}" Foreground="{DynamicResource ForegroundMutedBrush}" Margin="8,0,0,8" TextWrapping="Wrap">
                                        8 bugs fixed: RefreshFilesAsync try/finally, ClearFiles stops player, engine choice
                                        auto-saved, integer field validation, SelectedTabIndex wired, AddFolder try/catch,
                                        Cancel button for batch and copy, Delete and Clear stop media player.
                                        7 UX improvements: auto-search debounce, auto-switch to Retrieved tab, search
                                        pagination with Load More, settings auto-save (800ms debounce), rename presets
                                        with double-click, Processing Log tab, rename presets stored in config.
                                        10 new features: Cancel button, Undo Last Embed, Bulk Artwork Download, Export CSV,
                                        Export NFO (Jellyfin/Kodi), Duplicate Detector, Watched/Unwatched flag, Match Score
                                        badge, Processing Log tab (Tab 6), Behaviour settings panel.
                                    </TextBlock>

                                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource BaseText}" FontWeight="SemiBold" Margin="0,0,0,2">
                                        v1.2.1  ·  Build 8 — Responsiveness Fix (Large Folder Loading)
                                    </TextBlock>
                                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource BaseText}" Foreground="{DynamicResource ForegroundMutedBrush}" Margin="8,0,0,8" TextWrapping="Wrap">
                                        Fixed "Not Responding" freeze when loading large folders (1000+ files).
                                        All metadata reading (ReadMetadata, FileInfo, FilenameParser) now runs on
                                        background threads — the UI thread is never blocked. Files are added to the
                                        list in batches of 50 with Task.Yield() breaks so the window stays fully
                                        responsive throughout. Progress bar updates accurately at every chunk.
                                        Refresh button uses the same chunked non-blocking approach.
                                        Files already in the list are skipped on folder reload to avoid duplicate reads.
                                        ProgressValue now correctly raises IsProgressVisible so the bar appears and
                                        disappears in sync with actual activity.
                                    </TextBlock>

                                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource BaseText}" FontWeight="SemiBold" Margin="0,0,0,2">
                                        v1.2.0  ·  Build 7 — Smart Copy Engine + Multi-threaded Scan + API Persistence
                                    </TextBlock>
                                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource BaseText}" Foreground="{DynamicResource ForegroundMutedBrush}" Margin="8,0,0,8" TextWrapping="Wrap">
                                        FastCopy detection expanded — scans all user-profile subfolders for non-standard installs (e.g. C:\Users\Name\FastCopy).
                                        Auto engine now selects FastCopy for large files (over 500 MB) over TeraCopy for better raw throughput.
                                        TeraCopy and FastCopy CLIs fully corrected — proper /Close, /SkipAll, /auto_close, /force_start flags.
                                        Built-in copy engine fully rewritten: multi-threaded (CPU-scaled), 8 MB buffer, per-file retry with back-off, size verification.
                                        Progress bar now byte-accurate with live filename in status bar during each transfer.
                                        File list clears and rebuilds from the last selected folder after a successful transfer.
                                        Retry count and retry delay are now configurable per-user in the Settings tab.
                                        API keys (TMDB/OMDB) stay greyed out after restart — validated state is persisted to config.json.
                                        Folder scan uses PLINQ across all CPU cores — significantly faster for large libraries.
                                    </TextBlock>

                                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource BaseText}" FontWeight="SemiBold" Margin="0,0,0,2">
                                        v1.1.0  ·  Build 6 — Move/Copy Tab + Cast + Last Path + ID Lookup
                                    </TextBlock>
                                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource BaseText}" Foreground="{DynamicResource ForegroundMutedBrush}" Margin="8,0,0,8" TextWrapping="Wrap">
                                        Full cast list — removed 10-actor limit from TMDB credits.
                                        App remembers the last folder and file location across sessions.
                                        Embedded IMDB/TMDB IDs auto-populate the ID Lookup field when a file is selected.
                                        Move/Copy tab with TeraCopy and FastCopy detection — falls back to built-in 4 MB
                                        buffered engine if neither is found. Progress bar and status bar linked to transfers.
                                        RadioButton engine selector (Auto / TeraCopy / FastCopy / Built-in).
                                        Selected file count shown live in the Move/Copy tab.
                                    </TextBlock>

                                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource BaseText}" FontWeight="SemiBold" Margin="0,0,0,2">
                                        v1.0.0  ·  Build 5 — Media Player + Technical Info + Quality Fixes
                                    </TextBlock>
                                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource BaseText}" Foreground="{DynamicResource ForegroundMutedBrush}" Margin="8,0,0,8" TextWrapping="Wrap">
                                        Mini media preview player with play/pause/stop beneath cover artwork.
                                        Technical info panel shows file size, duration, container format, video codec,
                                        resolution, audio codec, channels, sample rate and bitrate.
                                        IMDB + TMDB IDs now properly embedded and read back using structured [VME:] markers.
                                        Filename parser fixed — trailing ( no longer appears in titles like "100% Wolf (".
                                        Progress bar in status bar tracks folder loads, batch search and batch processing.
                                        Delete File button with permanent-deletion confirmation dialog.
                                        Folder-load completion banner with file count and auto-search indicator.
                                    </TextBlock>

                                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource BaseText}" FontWeight="SemiBold" Margin="0,0,0,2">
                                        v1.0.0  ·  Build 4 — File Path Fix + Settings UX
                                    </TextBlock>
                                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource BaseText}" Foreground="{DynamicResource ForegroundMutedBrush}" Margin="8,0,0,8" TextWrapping="Wrap">
                                        Fixed "file not found" error after rename — FilePath now updates in-list after rename.
                                        API key fields lock after successful validation with ✏️ pencil to unlock.
                                        Green ✓ / Red ✗ flash on validation. IMDB/TMDB ID refinement in search.
                                        Version + build number shown in title bar, status bar, and Help tab.
                                    </TextBlock>

                                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource BaseText}" FontWeight="SemiBold" Margin="0,0,0,2">
                                        v1.0.0  ·  Build 3 — Toast Notifications
                                    </TextBlock>
                                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource BaseText}" Foreground="{DynamicResource ForegroundMutedBrush}" Margin="8,0,0,8" TextWrapping="Wrap">
                                        Animated slide-in toast notifications for rename success, rename failure, embed complete,
                                        and batch summary. Auto-dismiss with manual ✕ button.
                                    </TextBlock>

                                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource BaseText}" FontWeight="SemiBold" Margin="0,0,0,2">
                                        v1.0.0  ·  Build 2 — Filename Intelligence
                                    </TextBlock>
                                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource BaseText}" Foreground="{DynamicResource ForegroundMutedBrush}" Margin="8,0,0,8" TextWrapping="Wrap">
                                        FilenameParser: extracts clean Movie Title and Release Year from scene-release filenames
                                        (e.g. Commando.1985.1080p.BluRay → "Commando", 1985). Original Filename field added to
                                        Raw Data tab. Auto-search triggers on file select. Batch simultaneous metadata search.
                                    </TextBlock>

                                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource BaseText}" FontWeight="SemiBold" Margin="0,0,0,2">
                                        v1.0.0  ·  Build 1 — Initial Release
                                    </TextBlock>
                                    <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource BaseText}" Foreground="{DynamicResource ForegroundMutedBrush}" Margin="8,0,0,8" TextWrapping="Wrap">
                                        Full metadata read/write via TagLib#. TMDB + OMDB API integration. Batch folder processing.
                                        Dark/Light theme. Portable single-EXE with config.json in app directory.
                                    </TextBlock>

                                </StackPanel>

